The MIT license above covers the original code in this repository only.
Third-party and historical components are NOT covered by it:

- roms/mp3404.bin — the Texas Instruments MP3404 mask ROM as used in
  Parker Brothers Merlin (© 1978 Texas Instruments / Parker Brothers).
  Included for emulation/preservation; it is the same dump MAME uses.
  Copyright is retained by its owners; it is not licensed under MIT.
- web/assets/merlin.png — Merlin faceplate artwork derived from Bob
  Doyle's site theelectronicwizard.com. Used with attribution; rights
  remain with the original author.
- The TMS1100 interpreter descends from Dominic Thibodeau's
  (hotkeysoft) C++ TMS1000-family emulator via carledwards/merlin-tms1100.
- The Merlin R/O/K matrix mapping was read from MAME's hh_tms1k.cpp
  (MAME is GPL-2.0); only the factual wiring was used, no MAME code.

See README.md and docs/architecture.md for full credits.
